Usage: chown [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Change the owner and/or group of each FILE.

Note: On Windows, changing ownership requires the
SeTakeOwnership/SeRestore privileges, usually an elevated shell.
Use -h to modify a symbolic link itself, including dangling links.

OPTIONS:
  -c, --changes           like verbose but report only when a change is made
  -f, --silent            suppress most error messages
      --quiet             suppress most error messages
      --dereference       affect referent of each symbolic link
  -h, --no-dereference    affect symbolic links instead of referenced files
      --from ARG          change only from current owner/group
  -H                      traverse command-line symlinks to directories
  -L                      traverse every symlink to a directory
  -P                      do not traverse any symbolic links
  -R, --recursive         operate on files and directories recursively
      --reference ARG     use RFILE's owner and group
  -v, --verbose           output a diagnostic for every file processed
      --preserve-root     fail to operate recursively on '/'
      --no-preserve-root  do not treat '/' specially
      --help              display this help and exit
  -V, --version           output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
